@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.27
@changelog
  - Codename: Randy - I AM the Liquor!
  - New: Learn-HUD — dockable window listing the focused plug-in's UC1 control → parameter map; CS / BC tabs follow focus, NORM / OPT / CTRL layer badge, click-a-row + wiggle to learn. Toggle via the learn_hud_toggle built-in or the "Rea-Sixty: Toggle Learn-HUD" action (no Settings checkbox)
  - New: Learn-HUD right-click — text size + text colour (CS/BC or white); window size persists globally (default 500x500)
  - New: FX-Learn modifier layers (Normal / Option / Control) — a UC1 control carries three overlays (own param, invert, knob-travel, Display label); edit via the editor's layer tabs, use by holding Option / Control (enable in Settings → Device → Keyboard Options)
  - New: Focused-track panel "Use track colour" — draws the track name in its REAPER colour
  - Change: Inserts overlay now defaults to a clean outline — CS yellow, BC red, no fill
  - Fix: per-layer custom Display labels show correctly on the UC1 LCD, FX-Learn editor, Learn-HUD and focused-track panel — no more snap-back to the default name after a press / turn / release
  - Fix: modifier-layer mappings no longer lost when switching the FX-Learn edit domain (slot cache now stores overlays)
  - Fix: British / American spelling setting honoured in the focused-track panel menu
